  - id: 3
    fields:
    - title: Name
      value: Inland Empire
      type: 0
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Text
    - title: Pictures
      value: '[]'
      type: 3
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Files
    - title: Description
      value: 
      type: 0
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Text
    - title: IsPlayer
      value: False
      type: 2
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Boolean
    - title: Articy Id
      value: 0x0100000000000373
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: Technical Name
      value: Ntt_A7D9C574
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: IsNPC
      value: True
      type: 2
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Boolean
    - title: ShortDescription
      value: Hunches and gut feelings. Dreams in waking life.
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: LongDescription
      value: "\"COOL FOR: DREAMERS. PARA-NATURAL INVESTIGATORS. MENTAL CREATORS.\\n\\nInland
        Empire is the unfiltered wellspring of imagination, emotion, and foreboding.
        It enables you to grope your way through invisible dimensions of reality,
        gaining insight into that which sight can\u2019t see. What\u2019s really
        going? What do these enigmatic riddles mean for the world-fate?\\n\\nAt high
        levels, Inland Empire animates the inanimate. You\u2019ll have conversations
        with your clothing, conversations that may change the course of the investigation
        if you\u2019re not throw in the loony bin first. With low Inland Empire,
        however, you\u2019ll be void of imagination \u2013 and character. And then
        how will you shape the cosmos?\""
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: BlankPortrait
      value: False
      type: 2
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Boolean
    - title: color
      value: 3
      type: 1
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Number
    - title: SUBTABLE__AlternatePortraits
      value: 
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    spritePortrait: {fileID: 0}
    alternatePortraits: []
    spritePortraits: []
  - id: 4
    fields:
    - title: Name
      value: Savoir Faire
      type: 0
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Text
    - title: Pictures
      value: '[]'
      type: 3
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Files
    - title: Description
      value: 
      type: 0
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Text
    - title: IsPlayer
      value: False
      type: 2
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Boolean
    - title: Articy Id
      value: 0x0100000000000405
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: Technical Name
      value: MOT_Savoir_Faire
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: IsNPC
      value: True
      type: 2
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Boolean
    - title: ShortDescription
      value: Sneak under their noses. Stun with immense panache.
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: LongDescription
      value: "\"COOL FOR: ACROBATS. THEIVES. UNBEARABLE SHOW-OFFS.\\n\\nSavoir Faire
        urges you to be better than you are: it urges you to be disco. Slip by others
        in Samaran boxing style, then tumble out the back with unexpected acrobatics.
        It enables you to move silent footsteps, to groove to a good beat, and to
        lift useful evidence off perps without them noticing. It also makes you a
        cooler cop, whose athletic flair will certainly impress the citizenry.\\n\\nAt
        high levels, Savoir Faire will make you the King of Cool \u2013 which is
        as much to say, the most stylish douchebag in Revchol. Nobody will see you
        until you\u2019re ready to be seen; and then, they\u2019ll get the full treatment,
        whether they want it or not. At low levels, however, you\u2019ll be a bumbling,
        feckless cop unable to catch pair of keys thrown by your partner without
        losing an eye.\""
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    - title: BlankPortrait
      value: False
      type: 2
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Boolean
    - title: color
      value: 5
      type: 1
      typeString: CustomFieldType_Number
    - title: SUBTABLE__AlternatePortraits
      value: 
      type: 0
      typeString: 
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    spritePortrait: {fileID: 0}
    alternatePortraits: []
    spritePortraits: []
